# Repository Structure
- Foundation code must not depend on industry/domain packages.
- Shared behavior belongs in shared hooks/models/runtime, not copied into individual components.
- Public APIs must be intentionally exported from package entrypoints.
- Internal implementation files must not become public APIs accidentally.
- `example/` is the internal playground/debug/repro environment.
- `docs/` is the official developer documentation source.
- `component-hardening/` is the SSOT for machine-readable hardening state and evidence.
- `.component-hardening/` is a pointer-only compatibility shim (no duplicated contracts).
- `docs/engineering/component-hardening/` stores human-authored hardening standards entrypoints.
- Avoid circular dependencies between packages and component families.
